by Amoifr at 2026-07-12T16:55:15Z

Thanks @mtarld, that's exactly the nudge this PR needed. 🙏

Reworked along the lines of #64190: the hardcoded list is gone. `JsonEncoder` still only knows `json` out of the box, and extra JSON-based formats are opted into through a reserved context key, `JsonEncoder::FORMAT_VARIANTS` (`json_format_variants`):

```yaml
framework:
    serializer:
        default_context:
            json_format_variants: ['jsonapi', 'problem', 'hal']
```

No new config node needed — `SerializerPass` already binds `default_context` to every encoder.

Two upsides over the curated list, @dunglas:
- no infinite list of formats to maintain in core;
- no shadowing: `serializer.encoder.json` is tagged before userland encoders, so a core `jsonapi`/`hal` claim would quietly win over a third-party encoder registered at the same priority. Opt-in leaves API Platform & co. in charge of their own formats.

The trade-off: #60701 (`#[MapRequestPayload]` + `application/vnd.api+json`) now takes one config line instead of working out of the box. Happy to add a dedicated `framework.serializer.json_format_variants` node, or ship defaults, if you'd rather have it zero-config — the whitelist and I parted on good terms, I can always call it back. 😄

