On the design call, I would rather not add the option.

#64190 as merged is a cache-partition key for the generated JsonStreamer code, not format aliasing, so it is not the precedent it looked like.

More importantly, the encoder never sees the media type, only a format name, so configuring it with a per-app list puts the knowledge in the wrong place. The caller already has it: `RequestPayloadValueResolver::mapRequestPayload()` reads `$request->getContentTypeFormat()` and hands the result straight to the serializer. Normalising the format to its structured suffix there fixes #60701 with no new public option, nothing to misconfigure, and it covers `hal+xml` and `atom+xml` for `XmlEncoder` at the same time. It is also closer to the media type parsing @dunglas asked for in March than the opt-in list is.

Two constraints I checked while looking:

 * Normalise after the `acceptFormat` check, otherwise `acceptFormat: 'jsonapi'` stops matching.
 * `Request::getFormat()` returns exact `initializeFormats()` entries before falling back to the suffix, so `application/vnd.api+json` yields `jsonapi` and only unregistered `+json` types yield `json`. Getting the suffix format in the resolver will likely need a small helper on `Request`.

